{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787027420893732002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"vivacious-widish-indianabat","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"69265142a86c74500e081b40260c71e148821f7671dd6811c86e5c609a03afd9","event_uuid":"d4d88bbb-a4e2-4be0-b55f-91796be5e2e5","position":{"commit_sha":"77f3332ad5065558a57c1955536c516011fe691d","position":"1787027406115418001-d4d88bbb-a4e2-4be0-b55f-91796be5e2e5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e305cafc65c707a91dd792992a02aeda6beb6263863b73af4ac196cdaf909f2c","event_uuid":"0282fb77-6040-4415-b67a-bc93e566e23f","position":{"commit_sha":"2403c0fca1472871928a1074d2fd4cedf4f30129","position":"1787027416372919001-0282fb77-6040-4415-b67a-bc93e566e23f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"94ddc232ec91f80432a5f9326ff62c1cb0085859cb7300eda86fb4d23dcae315","event_uuid":"dff94f8f-925d-4e1a-91de-ac607243835b","position":{"commit_sha":"0a4e21ac0e26faec2ae255fe1291988005f1f818","position":"1787027420893732001-dff94f8f-925d-4e1a-91de-ac607243835b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787027406115418001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\nBinding persistence currently shares `binding_store.py` with lifecycle policy. Extraction is unsafe until byte layout, load rules, and ordered partial-state failure behavior have direct oracles.\n\n## Outcome\nCreate `BindingRepository` as the sole owner of live, retired, rotation, and alert files. It retains the original dictionaries and exact serialization behavior; no facade cutover occurs in this task.\n\n## Plan\n1. Start with direct failing tests over legacy and unknown-field fixtures, unchanged-save behavior, and exact sorted/indented/trailing-newline bytes.\n2. Implement path ownership, current corruption rules, open typed views over the original dictionaries, dirty gating, tempfile cleanup, and per-file `os.replace`.\n3. Add fault cuts for tempfile creation, rotation replace, retired replace, live replace, and alert write. Preserve rotation-before-live order, the newest inline rotation floor, and current raise/swallow behavior.\n4. Make no multi-file atomicity, journal, eager rewrite, deep-copy, or publication claim.\n\n## Testing\nRun the direct repository suite with real temporary files and injected filesystem cuts. Tests assert exact surviving bytes and exceptions, not implementation call counts alone.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Legacy and unknown-field fixtures round-trip to byte-identical sorted/indented/newline JSON with no eager write.\n- [ ] An unchanged unit of work performs no replacement.\n- [ ] Every named filesystem fault leaves the documented old/new file combination and preserves current raise/swallow behavior.\n- [ ] Rotation is attempted before live replacement, and rotation-save failure retains the newest inline floor for later convergence.\n- [ ] Repository views retain the original dictionaries rather than detached deep copies.\n\n## Out of scope\nFacade delegation, lifecycle extraction, tickets publication, and recovery cutover remain in later RP-02 tasks.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_repository.py","reason":"New byte-preserving persistence and unit-of-work owner."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_repository.py","reason":"Direct byte, corruption, dirty-gate, and fault-cut oracles."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","5142-4dbf-9469-4672"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"5142-4dbf-9469-4672","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp02","binding-store","tdd"],"ticket_id":"2c81-7119-fb6b-44b1","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-02 S1 T1 — Build the byte-preserving binding repository","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_repository.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC5","dd_text":"Repository byte contract, unchanged gate, fault cuts, ordering, and shared dictionary identity"}]},"source_event_uuids":["d4d88bbb-a4e2-4be0-b55f-91796be5e2e5","0282fb77-6040-4415-b67a-bc93e566e23f","dff94f8f-925d-4e1a-91de-ac607243835b"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787027420893732002,"uuid":"dc814cd9-2969-4201-aec0-1870a770ea2f"}